Z||000018||Eric||05-24-2001||11:04 AM||||I used to own an 89 Celica GT.  It was a nice car especially for a high school kid.  It wasn't terribly fast, but it was kind of quick compared to many other econoboxes.  It handled well.  Although it did everything well, it can't be compared with a V6 Fiero.  It just didn't have the guts our little cars have.  <P>The most recent race I was in was with a circa '93 Celica GTS.  Now the GTS model is the same as the GT except for a few cosmetic changes.  It has a 130 horse 2.2L motor.  It does the quarter in the low 16s, and 0-60 in 8 something with the manual transmission.  The car I raced had the manual, because I could see the nose dive at the shifts (she probably needed new shocks too).  The Celica girl pulled up on my left side, reved, and nudged the line before the intersection.  Well I kind of felt like playing too, so I moved up as well.  The light switched from red to green, she dropped the clutch, and with a bark from the front tires, she was off.  I just took all this in from a stop.  In fact, I think I let her wind out first gear before I even got on it.  All I did was launch gingerly, short shift into second, and let the torquiness of my 3.2 do the work for me.  I passed her is second at 50mph or so.  She did the typical ricer blow by, and I just sat back and laughed.||||reg||1
